When we doing scaling to millions of users, we are doing the onse user setup to millions of users. In last we are having the database sharding concept. So we will learning it in detail and see the Consistent Hashing-> this is one of the revolutionary concept of HLD. And we will be also learning about the load-balancers in detail. 

## Database Sharding :- 
- We are knowing the proper flow of the request in the client-server architecture, which includes client, LB, server-tier, DB-tier, and DNS. So in the DB tier we will be doing the sharding using Modulo function -> we find the hash-function and redirect to the database. -> we will be seeing the limitation of the modulo-function and then see how Cosistant hashing solve/overcome that problem. 

- Exploring the DB tier :- 
  - Earlier we are having the Single DB which has its configurtion like Ram and HD size. 
  - Do not get the confuse between the Replication and Sharding. 
   - Replication means Master-slave arichtecture, jaha aur DB bana denge of same size, ek copy bana denge. We will be making this because if one database is fail/ crash then we can save the  our data. 
   - In sharding, If having the large data then our DB will be fulled/ and all request will come to that DB only. In Sharding which is also called the Horizontal scaling in DB. -> Where we stored the large amount of data in different DB. Data ko ham different db mai store karke rakhte hai, kuchh amount ek data mai aur kuchh amount ek data. (Physically alag DB mai stored but logically single jaise he hote -> ModuloFunction will help doing so). 

- Hash methods --> Modulo Operator 
  - Discription of hashfunction : hash(value) = integer (where value may be string, integer, boolean,etc)
  - In hashing we will have been learnt about the working module operator in the distribution of the key. 
  - Key : A parmeter on which basis we stored the data in the DB/ hash. It may be integer, string, char, etc -> user ke baare any detail jo unique ho. 
   - key1:1, key2:2, key3:3, key4 : 4 ...
   - So let's they 1,2,3,4 are value of the id of table. Which is also called as sharding on the basis of which we divide the data and stored it in the different DB. 
   - So firstly, Bigger Database stored all the information -> It can handled the load then we shared the data. 
   - So Now have the DB1, DB2 and DB3 as the database. Now we want that logically ye same rahe then :- 
    - Now the request-response passes from the server -> LB(Hash/Function) -> [DB1 ,DB2, DB3] 
    - Hash function has modulo operator (%)
    - Let's see the working / data flow :- 
      - lets find hash(key0) = 0 then the resultant of hash function will be modulo with no. of database we have. 
      - modulo(%) because it gives the range between 0 to n-1. 
      - let indexes of database are 0 , 1, and 2. 
      - so key0 ka resultant value 0 tha so wo 0 index wale database mai store ho jayega.
      - so aise key ki basis par database mai value store hota jayega.  
      - We have different algorithum for to implementation this like we have an algorthum SHA-1(in criptography), which help in calculating different datatypes ka ek integer value nikal kear deta hai.
      - So we have done the post call till now in this section. so what if user want to access data from the database. 
       - Then we do the same steps we find out the hash value and then jo bhi hash value us database-index par chale jayenga aur waha ja kar data read kar lenge. 

    ### Limitation's of database sharding
    Horzontal scaling :- if database is loaded then  we can add the new database. And if database ko apne according use kar sake. If need then able to db if not needed then remove db. 
     - So when we add new database then our hashfunction -> calculation will be changes. Then we have to do the remigration of all the data. Because doing changes in the modulo function will affect the all rows. 
     - Database migration is very complex and try to avoid doing database migration. 

  - To avoid this limitation we have the concept consistent Hashing -> name suggest ek aisa consistant algorithum jo consistant ho. Means while scaling the database database migration kam se kam ho. Jayda data ko hamko move n karna pade. 
  - Database sharding is brute-force-technique and primitive techniqe for hashing technique. 
  - In sharding we want that all the database get hit/request/load  uniformly rahe. 

## Consistant Hashing :-
- So we have limitations in Hashing method due to the modulo operator. So we have to replace the modulo operator. 
- Consistant hashing includes three main concept :- 
  - Hash Ring
  - Db Hashing 
  - Keys Hashing 

- Hash Ring :- A ring which holds many value. Lets say the values lie b/w 1-100. We have just distribute the value over the ring -> just like cyclic array.
- Now we try to hash the different DB we have like DB1, DB2 ,DB3 and DB4. let's sharding key =IP address of DB. Let say that we have got the hash value (hash(IP)) between 1-100 range. 
 - So in charo DB ka, IP address ke according jo bhi value hamko mil raha hai us DB ko hashring par rakh denge. Lets say we got the value 1,25,50,75 for respectively databases we have. 
 - So we have our databases in the above two points. 
- Note :- Pahle ham Key ko hash kar rahe the lakin ab ham pahle database ko hash kardo then go for the key hashing. 

- Keys hashing :- 
 - We have the different keys such as key0=0, key1=1, key2=2, key3=4. 
 - find hashvalue : hash(key0) = 11 , hash(key1) = 41, hash(key2)=65 and so on 
 - ko bhi value aa rahi hai Hash ring us position par rakh do. 
 - So abhi tak keys ko sirf value mila hai hash ring ka, abhi server ka access nahi mila hai.So server assign karne ke liye ham key se clock direction mai ghumenge jo bhi pahla server milega waha us key ko assign kar denge. 

Advantage :- 
 - Only affected keys need to migrate :-   If introducing new database say it Db5 lets say its iska DBHashing ka value 90 hai, then Is DB ko 90 value par rakh denge hash ring mai. Ab hamko sabko keys ko migrate nahi karna padega jaha naya Db add kiya uske just pahle wala server se newserver  mai jo value tak jo bhi  keys hai unko move karna hoga. Similarly when any server/database go down then uske pahle wali database server ke baad wali keys ko next clock direction mai server par chali jayengi.
  - Database ke migration ko reduce karta hai. 

- Conclusion :- So isme ek hashRing lo, aur jo bhi db server hamare pass present hai unka hashvalue nikalo hashfunction ke help se using the databaseIP. And then point this db on on the basis of the hashvalue on the Ring hash. Then iske baad keys ka hashvalue nikalo then isko bhi point kardo HashRing par point kar do, ab key ke clock-direction mai jo bhi pahla Dbserver aata hai us key waha stpre kardo. 

limitations :- 
- Uneven distribution of the keys :- So when we introduce the hash function we try to take the hashfunction which takes uniformly distribute the keys. So in statixtices we have learnt about standard deviation, standard deviation should be minimized here. 
 - In criptography, we took that hash function, which is nearer or equal to prime number. Because prime no. uniformly distribute the data. If odd/even then it divided two parts mostly. 
 - So here we try to minimize the standard deviation, for uniformly distribution of data. Standard deviation state how unifornly data is distributed? 

- But this problem is not faced during the Modulo operator bases hashing because  modulo operator responsible for the hash's are distribute close to all DB.

- Celebrity problem (hotspot key problem) :- 
 - So lets say we are having instagram database server we designed below, which contains four database and each have two virtual nodes in the hashRing. 
 - lets say we have account of the celebrity, key4 : SRK, Key5 : Virat Kohli and Key6 : Ronaldo, se when find the hash value of these, all three comes to the same database. 
 - So our algorithum is equal for all the user's. If we put all the three in the same database then we know many of them like, comment, postvisit karte hai.
 - So we have to fatch the data again and agaian, basically load incresed. So hamare pass toh key limited aayi but wo keys -> high qurry/ fetch wali keys aa gayai ki load bad gayi. -> This problem is called hotspot key problem. 
 - virtual node ka concept is problem ko bhi solve kar deta hai. 

-> So we need to have the good hashfunction so that we have the uniform distribution of the data/keys along the databases. 

## Virtual Nodes (Replicas of Orginal nodes) :- 
- so hamare pass server bahut kam iske wajah se standard deviation high ho raha hai. So we let introduced the replica's of the four DB we have designed. 
- So let's create virtual node, which is the database but it is the replica's/copy of the database.
- So lets name the replica of DB1 as DB1_1 -> first virtual node.
  - The replica database has also some Ip address let's find out the hashvalue of that using its Ip address and locate them in hashRing. 
  - Similarly we introduced the one more virtual node of DB1 as DB1_2. (2nd virtual node of the DB1) and find out their hash value and located them in the hash ring. 
- Similarly saare database like DB2,Db3 and Db4 ke replica bana kar usko bhi hashRing mai locate kardo. 

-> By doing so we increase the no. of DBserver point in the hashRing. So they are such a order if the key's hashvalue is nearer then also can got other server's as the copy of the one Database is present at different location on the hashring so key may come to that point which also means ki wo Original database mai jayega jiska replica hamko mia hai.
 - Generally raste mai pahle ek he dukaan thi, ab hamne franchise bana ke aur bhi duaane khol li then -> Ab hamare reachablity to customer aur bad jayegi. 

Vitual Node :- 
 - In master-slave architecture, we have studied that we have one main server and we have multiple replica's of the database.

- In real-world we take the many replica's of the one server like 1000 of virtual node. and thr range of ring is also bigger. 
Note :- 
1. Try to use the good hash function 
2. Try to create more virtual node, so if the keys are nearer then also they got the different database. -> So the load distribution is low. 

- Database badane se ham sharding bada rahe hai, replica's badane se ham replication bada rahe hai. Sharding karne se load kam kar rahe database ka. Replica's/virtualNode karne se same data original database aur uske aur bhi replica's mai hoga. 
General Example : Ek kaam ham jisko char logo mai baat diya, single person ko 25 percent kaam karna hoga. Ek person ke baad two replica/ virtual node means single person two aur person ko hire kar liya to do same amount of work, lakin is tarah Main person ko jayda thaan nahi hua. 

- Jis tarah ki application hai uske according ham database/servers ko introduced karte hai hamare server par. 


## Load Balancer(LB) :- 
- Lies between client and server , it helps to distribute the upcoming request to different servers. 
- How LB know that which request has to send on which server? What happend and how LB know when any server is  down? and more. 

Application of Load Balancer :- 
- It is responsible for the
  Scalability, Availablity, Security and Responsiveness.

- Scalability :- 
  - So agar hamare pass bahut sare server hai, aur LB saari keys ko uniformly distribute karta hai, toh ham server ko easily scale kar sakte hai. -> Helps in AutoScaling, we will see in the algorithums. 
  - So LB is smart it know when application is required server or when to remove the server. 

- Availability :- 
  - In CAP theorem we studied that if the server is down then LB detect that server it will stop farwarding the request on that server. Means waha bhejega jaha request bhej sakte means availability badata hai. 

- Security :- 
  - So different 3rd parties LB are having some extra features are :-
    - Stop the DOS, DDOS attack. So in these attack multiple request send by the hacker, so LB is responsible for Distributing the request to multiple server, hence saved from the DOS and DDOS attack. 
  - It has some algorithums like firewalls -> iskp LB ke bahar he rakhte hai. So request ko Firewall ke through bhejte hai. So firewall identify the spammers. 

- Responsiveness :- 
  - Response Time / Time To First Bit(TTFB) :- Jab bhi koi request server par aaye then us request ko kitani jaldi process karke wapas as response bhej pata hai. Si LB request ko distribute kar deta hai then iske wajah se responsiveness bad jayegi -> jaldi se request process hoke wapas bhej paayenge. 
   - Server will be busy when multiple request come to that server. Resposiveness hamare thread pool ko achha rakhta hai, taaki multiple request parallely server par chal paaye. 


### Algorithum of Load-Balancer :- 
- We can divide the Algorithum of LB in two ways :- 
  1. Static LB :- Simple and have one algo on that basis they distribute the load 
  2. Dynamic LB :- Complex and also responisble for the server condition (loaded?)

1. Static LB's Algorithum :- 
  1. Round Robin Algorithum :- 
    - Structure 
      - LB
      - Server : s1, s2, s3
    
    - It sends the request in round robin order like pahle s1 then s2 ko and then s3 ko.
    - So this algo is not responsible for taking care of load on the server it just flow's their priniciple logic. 

    - Limitation :- 
      - Do not consider the load on any server and Easy to Implement. 

  2. Weighted Round-Robin 
   - Structure 
     - LB
     - Server : s1, s2, s3
  
   - This algorithum assign sum weight to each server such as s1:1, s2:5, s3:10. Weight may be anything depending upon the limitiation of the servers. 
    - For example if weight of s1 is 1 then if RAM of this server is 32 GB then s2 wight is 5 as have it means s2 ki RAM s1 se paach guna jayda. Similarly HardDisk le sakte, etc Basis par assign karte hai. 
    - Jiska jitna jayda weight wo utna jayda Request ko handle kar sakta hai. 
   
   - So isme LB balancer Weight ke according request bhejne lagta hai, so s1 ka weight 1 hai then isko 1 request bhejega aur aage bad jayega, next server ki weight 5 hai then next five request yaha then go further and so on.

  - Limitation :- 
    - Not consider the load of server, It like if the server is keep processing the past request then also it assign the request equal to the weight of the server. 

  3. Ip hashing :- 
   - Structure 
     - LB
     - Server : s1, s2, s3

   - Yaha request ka Ip address ka hash value nikalte hai, aur server ki indexing hoti hai let say s1:0, s2:1, s3:2
   - And iske hashvalue ke accoding ham server assign kar denge. (Let say internally Modulo algo and any algo can be apply here)

   - Limitation :- Each user will always get the same server. 
     - As we do not change the IP address of the client (not using VPN/proxy server). So if we send the request from our laptop then the IP of the laptop will not change then hashvalue value will also not change, then har baar hamko call same server par jayenge 
      - Due to this it become the Tightly coupled(StateFul Architecture) with server. 
  
  Note : These are the static load balancer algorithum we have. 
  